e/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183042}] :question/id #uuid "bd6f191d-dd25-52a7-91ee-5275c10c8293" :question/math-academy-id "q-29828" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt{x^{5}} + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{5}}}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233186 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8d0c3f56-ed74-5e4d-bb18-eac56541b5e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-113781" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[4]{x}-{x}^{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[4]{x}-{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{1/4}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{1/4+1}}{(\\frac{1}{4}+1)}-\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{(5+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{(6)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{5}}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80a672a5-9018-5a78-9672-cf47be4d95f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566608} {:answer/id #uuid "98e55f7b-e970-5ec1-8f87-371c4a6f55f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}-4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566663} {:answer/id #uuid "d87f3a3b-f1ff-5e22-81b2-679daf615e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566796} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4e8d2e-8e7f-55f8-887c-4c3c6d134e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{x}+4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566840} {:answer/id #uuid "f5261de7-027d-545e-bff9-4ea8c302891e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5261de7-027d-545e-bff9-4ea8c302891e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566855} :answer-field/id #uuid "f689fbb7-4820-549d-86af-2dc10f9a0677" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79aa6724-ce36-5977-907b-506fab54c4d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71169" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+4.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+4\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}x+4\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-3/2}\\text{d}x+4\\int {x}^{0}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3/2+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+4\\left(\\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right)+C \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {x}^{-1/2}+4x+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234303 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09d58888-0116-53f3-b47a-9d0d7153229f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71173" :question/problem "$\\int 2+\\frac{1}{{y}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2+\\frac{1}{{y}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int 1\\,\\text{d}y+\\int {y}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\int {y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y+\\int {y}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{y}^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right)+\\frac{{y}^{-5+1}}{-5+1}+C \\\\  & =2y+\\frac{{y}^{-4}}{-4}+C \\\\  & =2y-\\frac{1}{4{y}^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c412eada-9cf7-59a5-905e-0f6c0063eb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t^3}{3}-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c412eada-9cf7-59a5-905e-0f6c0063eb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t^3}{3}-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540856} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1f591a2-abaf-568b-95d2-b28ddb7d4b0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "836e24be-b58e-500b-bb05-e9b2030ce5e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-133291" :question/problem "Find $y(t),$ the antiderivative of ${y}^{′}(t).$\n\n$y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,C$" :question/worked-solution "We know that ${y}^{′}(t)={t}^{2}-2.$\n\nApplying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {t}^{2}-2\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t-\\int 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int {t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t-2\\int {t}^{0}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{{t}^{2+1}}{2+1}\\right)-2t+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-2t+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ebaae1-1b6f-54a0-9ee3-20ad6d94b297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566561} {:answer/id #uuid "75869535-6c65-5fee-b563-b5239aaa4910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566587} {:answer/id #uuid "949d1af7-fd39-55bc-bf6f-81a0c846d362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566654} {:answer/id #uuid "a1102e39-908b-5d4b-9cc6-16a7726229bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566676} {:answer/id #uuid "e18db342-254e-56c4-b18d-3e730f819b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1102e39-908b-5d4b-9cc6-16a7726229bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566676} :answer-field/id #uuid "abc76652-94ff-55a2-98b8-14e731f2dc71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e4827b1-c8af-5e0e-a92c-bab0c6f19c7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71167" :question/problem "$\\int 5-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int {x}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\left(\\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right)-\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}+C \\\\  & =5x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bd6e13b-e453-517b-905a-f7a3184b5e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t+\\frac{t^{7}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bd6e13b-e453-517b-905a-f7a3184b5e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t+\\frac{t^{7}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671060} :answer-field/id #uuid "23b81b98-ddee-5ebf-a2b4-d2474b1ec7fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10e82ee6-837f-5483-bbea-742bf32b5839" :question/problem "Given $y'(t)=-2+t^{6}$, find $y(t)$, the antiderivative of $y'(t)$.\n\n$y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,C$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $y'(t)=-2+t^{6}$.\n\nApplying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-2+t^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(-2+t^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -2\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t+\\int t^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -2\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+\\frac{t^{6+1}}{(6+1)}+C \\\\ &= -2t+\\frac{t^{7}}{7}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAny additive constant in an antiderivative can be absorbed into the displayed arbitrary constant $C$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "265d13c3-577d-5fac-a55b-51d15a808773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{t^{3}}{3}+6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "265d13c3-577d-5fac-a55b-51d15a808773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{t^{3}}{3}+6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671049} :answer-field/id #uuid "48da94e4-b9dd-5ebb-b7ec-06b9298abbe7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ced7f38-807e-5a63-8102-df1f51116f7a" :question/problem "Given $y'(t)=-t^{2}+6$, find $y(t)$, the antiderivative of $y'(t)$.\n\n$y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,C$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $y'(t)=-t^{2}+6$.\n\nApplying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-t^{2}+6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(-t^{2}+6\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -\\int t^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+6\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -\\frac{t^{2+1}}{(2+1)}+6\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= -\\frac{t^{3}}{3}+6t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAny additive constant in an antiderivative can be absorbed into the displayed arbitrary constant $C$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a90f9a-b732-5698-877a-1b43e8e0388a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671045} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1b62dd-ead9-5f02-9ef2-9d6c9b599c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671052} {:answer/id #uuid "3c5a129e-e655-5463-8fa5-e610d85ece00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671053} {:answer/id #uuid "c4400cd9-8fb9-5cc8-a124-a60e68afe4c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6t-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671065} {:answer/id #uuid "ce618bea-2ea8-5b4b-a24a-0b9b5645e22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6t-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c1b62dd-ead9-5f02-9ef2-9d6c9b599c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671052} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c239950-b48e-5c11-82f4-4fd02bd24fce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "392bd156-a25b-55e4-bce8-37c27fa38c55" :question/problem "Find the integral of $3+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{3}}}$ for $t>0$." :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(3+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{3}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(3+\\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= 3\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t+\\int t^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= 3\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+\\frac{t^{-\\frac{3}{2}+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+C \\\\ &= 3t-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671054 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f92e116-4a5d-5079-842a-052dddf334e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671056} {:answer/id #uuid "6d31b1a8-3f52-5e00-9f1c-497c8e2400c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+\\frac{x^{7}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671058} {:answer/id #uuid "a899a0ec-a01d-5fe6-b0a7-6adc5f0f285e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+\\frac{x^{7}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671063} {:answer/id #uuid "b329d488-d81c-5863-a1d3-b5fd0268822d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671064} {:answer/id #uuid "eb50de8c-ecdb-5560-895f-fa5d14eae046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x+\\frac{x^{7}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b329d488-d81c-5863-a1d3-b5fd0268822d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x+\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671064} :answer-field/id #uuid "01f4f87a-a45e-52f0-8489-eb5074709047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "420d5e76-0051-5ab1-a5d9-92d8e39b4f48" :question/problem "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(-6+x^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-6+x^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(-6+x^{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= -6\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &= -6\\frac{x^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+\\frac{x^{6+1}}{(6+1)}+C \\\\ &= -6x+\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a183bc35-1977-50a3-9ea8-d6135d3f1cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{t^{6}}{6}-5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a183bc35-1977-50a3-9ea8-d6135d3f1cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{t^{6}}{6}-5t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671061} :answer-field/id #uuid "7141dba1-52ab-5b56-8273-475b65054ed4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a43f7211-93e1-579c-98a5-37395b38f6c3" :question/problem "Given $y'(t)=-t^{5}-5$, find $y(t)$, the antiderivative of $y'(t)$.\n\n$y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,C$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $y'(t)=-t^{5}-5$.\n\nApplying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-t^{5}-5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(-t^{5}-5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -\\int t^{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-5\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -\\frac{t^{5+1}}{(5+1)}-5\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= -\\frac{t^{6}}{6}-5t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAny additive constant in an antiderivative can be absorbed into the displayed arbitrary constant $C$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule"}]
